  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "An array is called sortable if it can be sorted in non-descending order using the following operations several times (possibly 000 times):\n\n\nChoose index iii, and multiply AiA_iAi​ by −1-1−1.\nFor example, [3,2,1,1,2][3, 2, 1, 1, 2][3,2,1,1,2] can form [−3,−2,1,1,2][-3, -2, 1, 1, 2][−3,−2,1,1,2] which is sorted.\n\nYou are given an array of NNN positive integers - [A1,A2,…,AN][A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_N][A1​,A2​,…,AN​]. Find the number of pairs LLL and RRR such that\n\n\n1≤L≤R≤N1 \\le L \\le R \\le N1≤L≤R≤N\n[AL,AL+1,…,AR][A_L, A_{L + 1}, \\ldots, A_R][AL​,AL+1​,…,AR​] is sortable.\nIn short, the problem asks to find the number of sortable subarrays of AAA.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer NNN - the size of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput the number of sortable subarrays of AAA.",
    "constraints": [
      "2≤N≤3⋅1052 \\le N \\le 3 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤3⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤N1 \\le A_i \\le N1≤Ai​≤N"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n1 1 2 1",
        "output": "8",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere are a total of 101010 subarrays. Only (L,R)=(1,4)(L, R) = (1, 4)(L,R)=(1,4) and (L,R)=(2,4)(L, R) = (2, 4)(L,R)=(2,4) are not sortable. All the other 888 are sortable"
      },
      {
